From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:44:41 +0900
Subject: Screencast: no extra flip for GLES readback

Reading back through a framebuffer follows the same bottom-left convention on GLES as
glGetTexImage on GL; the extra GLES flip turned SHM screencasts upside down with Mesa's
freedreno on KGSL (docs/46). Unconditional since the round-2 fold (docs/72); it was gated
on an environment variable that was always set on the device. Not verified on other GLES
drivers.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [verify on another GLES driver before offering it upstream]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:recording.quicksetting
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/46
Origin: vendor
---
 src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h
index 0d83508..9538dc3 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h
+++ b/src/plugins/screencast/screencastutils.h
@@ -47,7 +47,10 @@ static void doGrabTexture(GLTexture *texture, QImage *target)
 
     const auto context = EglContext::currentContext();
     const QSize size = texture->size();
-    const bool invertNeeded = context->isOpenGLES() ^ (texture->contentTransform() != OutputTransform::FlipY);
+    // Reading back through a framebuffer follows the same bottom-left convention on GLES as
+    // glGetTexImage does on GL (seen with Mesa's freedreno on KGSL, docs/46): no extra flip for
+    // GLES. Not verified on other GLES drivers.
+    const bool invertNeeded = texture->contentTransform() != OutputTransform::FlipY;
     const bool invertNeededAndSupported = invertNeeded && context->supportsPackInvert();
     GLboolean prev;
     if (invertNeededAndSupported) {
